I know that when I found a crash bug in vanilla (on October 20 this
year), paxed had fixed it on NAO within a day; crash fixes are one of
the easiest changes to get into the variant of NetHack running on NAO.

(For people interested, the bug in question is being teleported onto a
sink by a quantum mechanic while in the middle of equipping levitation
boots.)

In general, looking at any part of the code in enough detail allows you
to find bugs in it. For instance, on 21 December this year, I was
looking at the multi-turn action code, and found a crazy corner case
while eating food that probably has never happened in a game. (Try
eating one of a stack of cockatrice corpses while in a stoning-resistant
form and engulfed by a purple worm. The effects depend on whether or not
you have a full inventory; if you do, in addition to the obvious
effects, the game will go and overwrite some random memory, although
it'll usually be deallocated memory and thus have no effect.) I don't
think that one's been fixed on NAO yet, but then, I haven't reported it
yet.

